.TH CMUXR 1 "2026-10-20" "cmuxr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmuxr \- console and Qt6 music player for DomeD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmuxr
.RB [ \-\-console | \-\-gui | \-\-tray ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-gui ]
.RB [ "\-\-floor on|off" ]
.RI [ cmus-options ]
.RI [ "--open FILE..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmuxr
retains the cmus ncurses player and adds an optional Qt6 interface,
system tray controls, and spectrum data for an OpenXR disco floor.
In an interactive terminal it starts the console interface; in a graphical
session without a terminal it opens the Qt6 player.
Without a display server it uses the console.
Qt6 is not required for console operation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-console
Start the console interface, with a tray companion when a graphical session is available.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gui
Start only the console interface, without importing Qt6.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open the Qt6 player. Start the console engine on a pseudoterminal if needed.
A repeated GUI launch raises the existing window.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start with the Qt6 window hidden when a tray is available.
Without a tray, open the window.
.TP
.BI "\-\-floor " on|off
Persistently enable or disable the XR floor effect.
When given without a launch option, save the preference and exit.
This preference does not itself start an XR renderer; use
.BR cmuxr-floor (1).
.TP
.BI "\-\-open " FILE...
Play local audio files or file URIs. Play the first selection and queue
additional files. Reuse an existing player and raise its graphical window.
The desktop entry advertises supported audio formats for DomeD's Default
Applications chooser. Selecting cmuxr there enables opening music files;
installation preserves existing defaults. Decoding support depends on the core plugins.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display launcher help and exit.
.PP
Other options are passed to the cmus engine. See
.BR cmus (1).
.SH GRAPHICAL CONTROLS
The tray menu provides Play / Pause, Stop, List, the XR floor switch, and Quit.
Clicking the tray icon opens the list. Closing the window hides it when a tray
is available; Quit stops the player.
.PP
Up and Down select tracks and wrap at the ends.
Space pauses or resumes. Enter plays the selection.
Right enters a directory or a selected track's directory.
Left opens the parent directory, or the library from a playlist.
The source selector opens the current playlist, library, or playing directory.
Mouse scrolling loads more entries and wraps at the ends.
.PP
The view defaults to ten visible entries and caches at most eight pages of
128 library or playlist entries. Directory playback creates a separate playlist
containing the directory's direct tracks, preserving existing user playlists.
.SH APPEARANCE
The Qt6 interface follows DomeD's light or dark scheme, accent, font, font size,
and chrome opacity. Appearance changes are polled while the player runs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmuxr/
Player configuration and library. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/cmuxr/ .
.B CMUS_HOME
can override the engine configuration directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmuxr/settings.json
Frontend settings. The boolean
.B floor_enabled
controls the effect; the integer
.B visible_entries
sets the compact view height from 4 to 20 entries.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dome/appearance.json
DomeD appearance settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cmuxr-socket
Engine control socket. Override with
.BR CMUS_SOCKET .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cmuxr-floor.json
Versioned spectrum frames, updated up to 20 times per second.
The bridge also runs for console-only sessions.
.PP
Without XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, console runtime files use a private per-user directory
under /tmp. The XR renderer requires XDG_RUNTIME_DIR for spectrum transport.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Determine graphical session availability.
.TP
.B CMUS_HOME, CMUS_SOCKET
Override the engine configuration directory and Unix control socket.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Select configuration and runtime directories.
.TP
.B PULSE_SINK
Select a PulseAudio or PipeWire-Pulse output when using the ALSA pulse device.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cmuxr --console
cmuxr --no-gui
cmuxr --gui
cmuxr --floor off
cmuxr-floor --size 3x3
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmuxr-floor (1),
.BR cmus (1),
.BR cmus-remote (1),
.BR cmus-tutorial (7)
